  "final_message": "I put `channel` back, so the working tree now matches the original base commit `b02ef51`. The diff against `b02ef51` is empty. I haven't run CI itself. Locally, `npm test` passes (39 tests) and typecheck is clean.\n\n`channel` isn't unused: analytics-ingest requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`) under the ARCH-4 contract check. That consumer contract isn't in this repo, so I missed it when I removed the field. The event is built from `order.channel`, which comes from the request. Restoring the event field meant restoring all of it:\n- **Model and input:** `Order`, `NewOrder`, `CHANNELS` and the channel validation are back.\n- **API:** `POST /orders` reads and validates `channel` again.\n- **Tests and docs:** the tests and the example in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md` are back too.\n\n- **Commit on `main`:** HEAD is now `5e535ad \"gen\"`, which contains the earlier removal. I couldn't run `git checkout` here (the sandbox blocked it), so I reverted by hand. The restore is uncommitted, so the working tree differs from `5e535ad`.\n- **Typo:** one of my restoring edits dropped a space in `order.ts` (`OrderStatus =\"placed\"`), and I fixed it.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, the analytics-ingest team needs to drop that requirement from their contract first. After that, removing it from the event and model is safe.",
